**assistant**:
> ## The Arcane Library’s Three Wards
> 
> The library is protected by **The Trial of the Living Flame**. It is not meant to kill intruders—only to turn away the greedy, careless, or cruel. A bronze door says:
> 
> > “Bring warmth without ruin.  
> > Know truth beyond appearances.  
> > Stand when the world pushes back.”
> 
> The trials can be completed in any order. Each success lights one of three symbols on the door: a flame, an eye, and a mountain.
> 
> ### 1. Test of Heat — *The Ember Bridge*
> A stone bridge crosses a glowing lava-like mist. The heat is uncomfortable, but the real danger is that panicked travelers make the flames rise.
> 
> - **Goal:** Carry a small magical coal across without letting it flare out or explode.
> - **Checks:** DC 12 **Constitution save** to endure heat, or DC 12 **Animal Handling / Survival / Arcana** to understand the fire’s rhythm.
> - **Team solution:** One person shields the coal, another calls out safe stepping-stones, and another can use water, wind, or magic creatively.
> - **Lesson:** Fire is strongest when controlled, not simply fought.
> - **Failure:** Everyone takes only 1d4 fire damage and is gently pushed back to retry. No death or serious punishment.
> 
> ### 2. Test of Mind — *The Hall of Borrowed Stories*
> Books float in a circular room, each whispering a different “fact” about the party. Three books contain clues to the library’s location records; the others are convincing lies.
> 
> Examples:
> - “The loudest voice is always correct.”
> - “A dragonborn cannot be trusted.”
> - “A Titan grows only by crushing smaller things.”
> - “Ask what a book wants you to believe.”
> 
> - **Goal:** Identify the three truthful books.
> - **Checks:** DC 12 **Investigation, Insight, Arcana, or History**.
> - **Roleplay answer:** A player may simply explain why a statement is unfair, suspicious, or contradictory.
> - **Twist:** The best clue is found by listening to a book everyone else ignores: a tiny children’s storybook.
> - **Lesson:** Wisdom means questioning easy answers.
> 
> ### 3. Test of Body — *The Turning Mountain*
> The final chamber is an obstacle course of shifting stone: climbing walls, swinging platforms, a narrow beam, and a huge sealed stone wheel.
> 
> - **Goal:** Get the whole team across; the exit opens only when nobody is left behind.
> - **Checks:** DC 11 **Athletics** for climbing/lifting, **Acrobatics** for balance, or creative spells/tools.
> - **Ekemon moment:** He can hold the stone wheel in place or catch someone who slips.
> - **Varkash moment:** He can brace a bridge or use dragonborn toughness to cross a dangerous section.
> - **Druid moment:** Vines, animal forms, or clever nature magic can create a safe route.
> - **Lesson:** True strength protects others.
> 
> ## Reward: The Librarian’s Welcome
> When all three symbols shine, the door opens and a spectral librarian appears:
> 
> > “Heat without cruelty. Thought without pride. Strength without selfishness. You may seek knowledge here.”
> 
> The party receives **three glowing Library Seals**, each usable once to gain advantage on a relevant check inside the library.
